I don't feel a need for changing my .nethackrc around, I prefer having
my class and other such stuff random and the rest of the configuration
options static.

However, in case I some day happen to feel like checking how the game
looks with tiles, I have an alternative config file .nethackrc.x11 and 
a script I named nhx that looks like this:

#!/bin/sh
if [ -n "$DISPLAY"  -a  -f $HOME/.nethackrc.x11 ] ; then
    NETHACKOPTIONS=$HOME/.nethackrc.x11
fi
exec nethack "$@"

No need to actually swap the config files around, when all you really
need to do is change the NETHACKOPTIONS environment variable to point
to another file..

